        - rid: 9198629236872577130
        - rid: 9198629236872577131
        - rid: 9198629236872577132
        <Notes>k__BackingField:
        - <Pos>k__BackingField: {x: 10180, y: 10540}
          <RawContent>k__BackingField: '<p>We''ve given dialogue starting elements
            a custom element attribute:</p><p><strong>tag: dialogue_start</strong></p><p>This
            way, the game engine knows where to look for each NPC''s dialogue start.</p><p><em>We''ve
            used this solution in the Unreal Engine demo game.</em></p><p>Right click
            the element and choose "Properties," to see it.</p>'
          <ColorTheme>k__BackingField: cyan
        - <Pos>k__BackingField: {x: 11480, y: 10620}
          <RawContent>k__BackingField: '<p>Just as with dialogue starts, we''ve given
            <strong>dialogue ending elements</strong> a custom element attribute:</p><p><strong>tag:
            dialogue_end</strong></p><p>This way, the game engine knows not to follow
            the [Back] connections, which are for Arcweave''s Play Mode playability
            only.</p><p>Right click these elements and choose "Properties," to see
            the tag attribute.</p>'
          <ColorTheme>k__BackingField: cyan
    - rid: 9198629236872577095
      type: {class: Board, ns: Arcweave.Project, asm: Assembly-CSharp}
      data:
        <Id>k__BackingField: 449db8e2-4a21-4a73-aece-f0435e7319fb
        <Name>k__BackingField: Starting Board
        <Nodes>k__BackingField:
        - rid: 9198629236872577133
        - rid: 9198629236872577134
        - rid: 9198629236872577135
        - rid: 9198629236872577136
        - rid: 9198629236872577137
        - rid: 9198629236872577138
        <Notes>k__BackingField:
        - <Pos>k__BackingField: {x: 9760, y: 10340}
          <RawContent>k__BackingField: <p>This is the starting element for Arcweave's
            Play Mode. The game engine should ignore this.</p>
          <ColorTheme>k__BackingField: blue
        - <Pos>k__BackingField: {x: 10700, y: 10460}
          <RawContent>k__BackingField: "<p>These are the elements that the game engine
            must look for:</p><p>1. They are in the <strong>Starting Board</strong>
            (which has custom id: <strong>starting_dialogue_elements</strong>\u2014see
            board's properties).<strong><br></strong>2. They have the relevant NPC's
            <strong>character component</strong> attached.</p><p><em>We are using
            this solution in the Godot &amp; Unity demo games.</em></p>"
          <ColorTheme>k__BackingField: pink
    - rid: 9198629236872577096
